<p>A document created in an application will be superimposed with the Overlay 
 Data created separately, and then printed. This function is called Overlay.</p>
<p>For printing with the Overlay function, an Overlay Data file and Overlay 
 Setting must be created in advance.</p>
<p class="Graphic"><img alt="" class="help-img" height="200" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/ConceptOverlay.gif" width="330"/> </p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading">1. Overlay Data:</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">This is the image data for superimposing, which 
 is saved in the Overlay format.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading">2. Overlay Setting:</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">An Overlay Data file is combined with the setting 
 details (such as how and which page Overlay Data is superimposed on), 
 named, and registered as a set. Each set registered is called an Overlay 
 Setting.</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">When printing with Overlay, select an Overlay Setting 
 with the setting details, and the method and page that you prefer the 
 image to be superimposed on.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading">3. A document to be printed:</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Using an application, create a document to be printed 
 with the Overlay Setting.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading">4. Print result:</p>
<p class="Normal-indent">The document is printed with the Overlay Setting.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Superimposing data will be aligned with the document 
 page at the upper left corner. If the document to be printed and superimposing 
 data differ in size and orientation, the superimposing data might be cut 
 or protrude.</p></li>
<li><p>Depending on the application, you might not get 
 the expected result.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2>Creating a New Overlay Data File</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Setup</span> menu 
 of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Save as Overlay Data</span> 
 in the <span class="Term-Soft">Job Type:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span> 
 to open a dialog box and select the destination to save the overlay data.<br/>
 Enter the file name for the "rpo" overlay data file.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-OS">Save</span> to save 
 the new overlay data and close the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2>Overlaying Printing Documents with Overlay Data</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Add Overlay</span> 
 check box. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit...</span> to open a dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Enter the name of the Overlay Setting in the <span class="Term-Soft">Name:</span> box.<br/>
 To edit a registered Overlay Setting, select the name of the overlay 
 setting in the <span class="Term-Soft">Overlay Data:</span> list.</p></li>
</ol>
<ol start="5">
<li><p>In the <span class="Term-Soft">Path/File Name:</span> 
 box, enter the path and file name for the Overlay Data file or click <span class="Term-Soft">Browse...</span> to select the file you want to use as 
 the Overlay Data .</p></li>
<li><p>To print the Overlay Data in the front, select 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Bring to Front</span> check box. The image under 
 the Overlay Data will not be visible.</p></li>
<li><p>To superimpose the Overlay Data on the first page 
 only, select the <span class="Term-Soft">First Page Only</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>After specifying the settings, click<span class="Term-Soft"> 
 Add</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span> to save the setting.<br/>
 If you click <span class="Term-Soft">Update</span>, a dialog box appears 
 asking if you want to overwrite the old overlay setting. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p>You can select a registered Overlay Setting in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Overlay Data:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu. </p></li>
<li><p>To print the same overlay data using different 
 setting configurations, provide each of the available data combinations 
 with its own overlay data name and register those names in advance.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<h2>Deleting an Overlay Setting</h2>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Effects</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Add Overlay</span> 
 check box. Click <span class="Term-Soft">Edit...</span> to open a dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select an Overlay Setting from the <span class="Term-Soft">Overlay 
 Data:</span> list, and then click <span class="Term-Soft">Delete</span>. 
 </p></li>
<li><p>A dialog box appears prompting for confirmation. 
 Click <span class="Term-Soft">Yes</span>.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
